Protocol provenance
===================
Each parameter is traced to (a) the paper it comes from, page-checked against the author-posted PDFs
(references/), and (b) the code implicit.harvard.edu runs, pinned in upstream/minno-tasks:
  IAT/iat11.js                                   the IAT task the live Race IAT loads
  scorer/nogaScorer.js, scorer/feedbacker.js     its scorer and feedback rules
  docs/studies/datapipe.iat.examples/demo.iats/  the demo site's task configs (race.js ...)
  docs/studies/raceiat/raceiat_instructions.jst  the pre-IAT instructions page

Observed on the live site (a browser HAR of the Race IAT, 2026-10-30): the study demo.us/demo.race.0006
loads cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/baranan/minno-tasks@0.*/IAT/iat11.js and .../scorer/nogaScorer.js, and the
copies served were byte-identical to upstream/minno-tasks at the pinned commit.  Its site-hosted files
(not redistributed here) and their sha256:
  user/demo.us/demo.race.0006/raceiat.js        2fecdcfa9c469e71f013d2933f4e2ecc5191630d647a0a40a32b9c50635e1e96
  user/demo.us/demo.race.0006/mgr.js            12c122b0b47c01667973fe580e0a7843b721b60bc1b82c02e46b814dfe62f4d3
  user/demo.us/demo.race.0006/instiat_race.jst  339019080349c16ee98015023e05075582809b5a3ccb9a1ae5f364693b6c8872
  user/demo.us/demo.race.0006/realstart.jst     2ddd06fc7c8fed43ea032f3416f405c1d76944c384588a429321bfe731ebbe40
raceiat.js has the same faces as demo.iats/race.js and no parameter overrides; mgr.js has the same
label sets and the same 32+32 attribute words; instiat_race.jst has the same text as
raceiat_instructions.jst.  IAT/iat10.js and IAT/qualtrics/quiat9.js (Qualtrics) are earlier variants:
same procedure, but a single-parcel D with a 150 ms fast flag (printed here as D_single_parcel).
Citations: references/papers.bib.

